 An empty ATA channel answers 0xFF or 0x00 depending on what drives the bus,
 and neither can come from a present drive. 0xFF is the ISA bus floating with
 nothing on it: it asserts BSY, DRQ and ERR at once, so a wait that spins until
 BSY clears never finishes. 0x00 has DRDY clear, so a wait that spins until
 DRDY sets never finishes. codex-vm answers 0x00 on the two status ports when
 no disk is attached (`codex-vm.c`, `ide_handle_in`, the `!d->present` arm) and
 0xFF on the rest, so a check for only one of the two passes on hardware and
 hangs on the bed, or the reverse.

  ata-status-floating : Integer = 255

  ata-status-empty : Integer = 0
